==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sel-}}
Recorded since 1432 as {{inh|en|enm|resulten}}, from {{der|en|la-med|resulto|resultare}}, in Classical {{der|en|la|-}} "to spring forward, rebound", the frequentative of the past participle of {{m|la|resilio||to rebound}}, from {{m|la|re-||back}} + {{m|la|salio||to jump, leap}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈzʌlt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-result.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌlt|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|re|sult}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[proceed]], spring up or rise, as a [[consequence]], from facts, arguments, premises, combination of circumstances, consultation, thought or endeavor.
#: {{syn|en|attend|obtain|issue|follow|arise|ensue}}
#* {{RQ:Tillotson Works|sermon=IV|passage=Pleasure and peace do naturally '''result''' from a holy and good life.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|followed by "in"}} To have as a consequence; to [[lead]] to; to [[bring about]].
#: {{ux|en|This measure will '''result''' in good or in evil.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=October 23, 2011|author=Phil McNulty|work=BBC Sport|title=Man Utd 1-6 Man City|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/15325536.stm|passage=United's hopes of mounting a serious response suffered a blow within two minutes of the restart when Evans, who had endured a miserable afternoon, lost concentration and allowed Balotelli to steal in behind him. The defender's only reaction was to haul the Italian down, '''resulting''' in an inevitable red card.}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|year=2013|month=May-June|author=[http://www.americanscientist.org/authors/detail/katrina-g-claw Katrina G. Claw]|title=Rapid Evolution in Eggs and Sperm|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/feature/2013/3/rapid-evolution-in-eggs-and-sperm|volume=101|issue=3|magazine=w:American Scientist|passage=In plants, the ability to recognize self from nonself plays an important role in fertilization, because self-fertilization will '''result''' in less diverse offspring than fertilization with pollen from another individual.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20170609053207/http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/feature/2013/3/rapid-evolution-in-eggs-and-sperm|archivedate=9 June 2017}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|legal}} To [[return]] to the [[proprietor]] (or heirs) after a [[reversion]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive|obsolete}} To leap back; to [[rebound]].
#* {{RQ:Homer Pope et al Odyssey|book=XI|passage=the huge round stone, '''resulting''' with a bound}}

